// Gala noise models as typed values.
// This library provides noise model builders that create backend configurations.
//
// These are compiler builtins (declarations without bodies) that bind to runtime
// noise model constructors. The `Backend` type is not directly user-visible;
// instead, these functions return backend values that can be passed to `run(f, on: backend)`.
/// Create a simulator backend with depolarizing noise.
/// `p` is the probability of a Pauli error (X, Y, or Z each with p/3) after each gate.
fn depolarizing(p: Float) -> Backend quantum;

/// Create a simulator backend with readout error.
/// `p` is the probability of flipping the measurement outcome (0↔1).
fn readout_error(p: Float) -> Backend quantum;

/// Create a simulator backend with combined depolarizing and readout error.
fn combined_noise(depolarizing_p: Float, readout_p: Float) -> Backend quantum;